# ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  THIS FILE IS COMMITTED TO A PUBLIC REPO. NEVER PUT REAL VALUES HERE.     │
# │                                                                          │
# │  Copy it first, then fill in the copy:   cp .env.example .env.local      │
# │  Next.js loads .env.local — it does NOT load this file, so real values    │
# │  placed here don't work locally AND risk being committed.                │
# │                                                                          │
# │  Pasting into the Vercel dashboard? Paste the RAW value with no quotes.   │
# │  Quotes are stripped from .env files but kept verbatim by Vercel, which   │
# │  shows up as "WRONGPASS invalid or missing auth token".                   │
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Required for the Ask-Me-Anything chat. Get one free at aistudio.google.com.
# Without it the site still renders in full; only the chat degrades to an
# inline "email me instead" card.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Rate limiter for the public chat endpoint (free tier at upstash.com).
# The route refuses to serve chat in production if these are missing — a public
# LLM endpoint with no limiter is an open invoice.
#
# You do NOT need a dedicated database. The limiter namespaces its keys with an
# "ama:" prefix, so it can share an existing Upstash Redis with other apps.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# Portfolio photo and résumé, hosted on UploadThing rather than committed to
# this public repo — the raw files were never meant to be clonable. Without
# these, the site falls back to public/portfolio-image.jpg and
# public/shlok-iyer-resume.pdf on disk (both gitignored — present for local
# dev, absent from the repo and from any GitHub-integration Vercel build).
# No NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix needed: both are only ever read by server
# components (PhotoPlate, the Contact page), so the resolved URL reaches
# the browser baked into the rendered HTML, not through the client JS
# bundle. Just static UploadThing file URLs — no UploadThing API/secret
# key needed anywhere in this app.
PORTFOLIO_IMAGE_URL=
RESUME_PDF_URL=

# Optional. Gates the deep health check (/api/health?deep=1&key=...), which
# pings Redis and returns raw upstream error text. Without this set, deep
# mode is disabled entirely (fails closed) and only the plain up/down check
# is public. Generate any random string, e.g.: openssl rand -hex 32
HEALTH_CHECK_SECRET=
